  "prompt_text": "The figure presents a broad pathway from plant microbiome functions to One Health benefits and then to selected Sustainable Development Goals. On the left, microbes associated with plant roots are shown as key helpers of plant performance. Their visible roles include boosting growth and yield, protecting plant health, improving nutrient quality, increasing resilience to stresses, reducing agrochemical use, improving soil health, protecting biodiversity, and lowering contamination.\n\nThese functions feed into a central One Health framework. A large triangle links food and feed security, environmental health, biodiversity, sustainability, performance, and well-being. Inside it, a circular diagram places “One health” at the center and connects healthy plants, healthy diet, healthy animals, healthy humans, and healthy soils. The overall message is that managing the plant microbiome can create benefits that move from crops and soils through livestock and diet to human health, while also supporting environmental integrity.\n\nOn the right, the figure ties these outcomes to several SDGs, especially zero hunger, good health and well-being, decent work and economic growth, industry and innovation, responsible consumption and production, climate action, life below water, life on land, and partnerships.",
